[Music]  the movie trilogy by peter jackson went  down in history and the book series by  j.r.r tolkien  is unrivaled anyway clearly we're  talking about the lord of the rings  after the last lord of the rings movie  was released in 2003 and the hobbit  trilogy has been concluded more than  seven years ago  it's about time for new content that's  what amazon thought in 2017  and so they embarked on one of the  biggest serious projects of  all time namely its own the lord of the  rings series  how big it is what it has to do with the  film trilogy and what you can expect in  general  is what we're presenting to you today in  our latest original so  enjoy our new episode  naturally the first point of discussion  is the storyline as we already know this  series will not be a remake of a former  story and will stand completely on its  own two feet  there will be a clear gap of about three  thousand years between frodo's  adventures and the upcoming series which  is why we can definitely speak of a kind  of prequel smart fans of the franchise  will know that we're in the so-called  second age of middle-earth  the most significant evidence for this  are a total of four maps of middle earth  officially published on twitter  which disclose some information about  the setting for example you can  recognize the fortress of minnesota  which was taken in the year 2002 of the  third age and subsequently named minis  morgul  another place marked on the map is  mini-sanor the capital of gondor which  was later renamed to minas tirith and  has existed since the year 3220 in the  second age  you can also see the small island of  tall fellas at the lower end of the  coast it was destroyed after the  numenoreans were wiped out in the second  age and as a result it became  barren and very hilly as can also be  seen on the map if you look closely  so there is enough proof that there are  thousands of years between the series  and the film trilogy at the beginning of  this year the fan page of the  onering.net  also revealed their first official  synopsis which was actually confirmed by  amazon via twitter  according to the synopsis amazon is  reawakening the heroic legend of the  legendary second age  the series is meant to take the vero  back to an era of great powers falling  and rising kingdoms as well as unusual  heroes and reveal the greatest  villain ever to come out of talking  spanning of course we all know who's  meant right here nearly none other than  sauron himself the synopsis goes on to  say that the evil will grow stronger in  a time of peace and that it will have to  deal with an ensemble of old and new  characters  in addition more or less the whole world  of middle earth will be explored  in this regard there are again a few  theories one of them being that we can  mainly expect breathtaking high seas  adventures  this is not unlikely after all the  island kingdom of numenor is located in  the far  south west of the map in a place only  ships can reach by sea moreover the plot  of the first of probably five seasons  will be told in eight episodes of still  unknown length we are definitely looking  forward to more updates concerning the  plot and the setting and will of course  keep you up to date in our weekly news  the cast is also not to be neglected of  course  at least three returning characters who  are officially confirming their roles  will be seen in the series  on the one hand there is the elf  galadriel who is no longer embodied by  kate blanchet but instead by  morphit clark she's certainly one of the  best known figures from middle earth and  now gets a clear rejuvenation thanks to  the 32 year old clark  the elf elrond and the villain sauron  are also part of the cast but without  any official confirmation  of the respective actors it is also very  likely that sauron s once in the book  will make use of his ability  as a shape shifter one of these guys is  the character anataro comes across as  very friendly  but only serves the sole purpose of  convincing the elves to forge the rings  as already hinted at the majority of the  cast consists of relatively unfamiliar  faces though there's marcella cavanaugh  who is expected to assume the new rule  of tyra as well as joseph molly who may  play the villain orrin  additionally there is robert aramaiya  who will probably take on the main role  of beldore  among many others just as with peter  jackson's trilogy they chose beautiful  new zealand as the filming location  unfortunately as with many other  productions not all went smoothly due to  the pandemic  filming had to be passed temporarily so  that up to 800 crew members had to be  sent home while production was at a halt  for  weeks for a project that is supposed to  cost over 1 billion us dollars already  this is of course no cakewalk happily  however production was resumed as soon  as possible and  is still in full swing the responsible  parties behind the camera are to begin  with  john d payne and patrick mckay who both  serve as serious developers and are the  creative minds behind the project  juan antonio baiona was responsible for  directing at least the first two  episodes with wayne yep and charlotte  branstrom assuming the director's  position in the following episodes  who's definitely not making a comeback  is peter jackson who refused to take a  leading position in the production  he will merely serve an advisory role  another interesting aspect for fans is  the budget which was briefly alluded to  earlier with an estimated 1 billion us  dollars the lord of the rings series  will be the most expensive series  production of  all time the filming rides alone are  said to have cost 250 million us dollars  on the other hand amazon will certainly  be receiving a nice amount of cash from  the new zealand government  since the streaming giant is entitled to  an estimated 116 million us dollars from  a national film funding scheme thanks to  the jobs  it generates locally  the release date of the series is still  an unanswered question for many fans  although shooting is slowly reaching its  end it is still not really certain when  the series will be available on amazon  prime video a release in the fourth  quarter of 2021 would be feasible which  would coincide perfectly with the cold  fall months  we also consider a later release in 2022  to be realistic as everything depends on  how smoothly filming goes on  as well as how many scenes need to be  reshot and so forth  in this regard we also hope to be able  to tell you a more exact time frame  soon that's it again with our latest  original episode  we hope you're now up to date on the  latest news and that you may even have a  little more anticipation for the  upcoming amazon series  feel free to write us in the comments  what you expect from the series and  subscribe to our channel if you want to  see more similar content  in the future thanks for watching and  see you next time  you

